    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nHi. The way I like to use Mini Sessions is to automatically load my session when one is available, so I have the `autoread` option enabled. I'm also using local session files. The problem is, I get a warning log whenever I open neovim when there is no session to load. It says:\n\n```\n(mini.sessions) There is no detected sessions. Change configuration and rerun `MiniSessions.setup()\n```\n(Also notice how the closing back-tick is missing)\n\nThe way I'd like it to work, is to silently skip loading a session if there isn't one. I'm not sure if this would work well with other use-cases, though.",
