        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nAlthough not showing the message is a reasonable solution, it is not *quite* addressed to resolve this use case. The `config.autoread` is hard coded to [read \"default\" session](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/68d4478920c7afdfa21c13706464e275d9ce3255/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L79) (local if present, latest global otherwise).\n\nMy suggestion would be to manually autoread only local session. With something like this:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup()\nlocal autoread_local = function()\n  -- Autoread only if detected local session and Neovim is started without args\n  if not (MiniSessions.detected['Session.vim'] and vim.fn.argc() == 0) then return end\n  MiniSessions.read('Session.vim')\nend\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimEnter', { once = true, nested = true, callback = autoread_local })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-11-11T11:45:43Z",
